# Cursor Agent — Development vs Operations Separation

## Cursor MAY (auto, no ops approval loops)

- Edit/create source, config, docs
- `npm run test:pipeline` / unit tests / `npm run build`
- git commit + push to backup branch when the task includes Git

## Cursor MUST NOT run during agent sessions

- `node scripts/run-pipeline-worker.mjs` / `run-pipeline.ps1` (operational intake)
- Windows Task Scheduler register / update / check loops
- Supabase operational INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on live catalog/pipeline data
- migrations / ad-hoc operational SQL writes
- Anything that triggers repeated Pending approval for ops

## Operations owner

- Fixed Task: `KBeautyMatch-Pipeline`
- Fixed command: `node scripts/run-pipeline-worker.mjs` (via `scripts/run-pipeline.ps1`)
- Limits/mode: `config/pipeline-operation.json` + optional overrides
- Humans: review `needs_review` only

## If scheduler args must change once

- Keep `scripts/update-pipeline-task.ps1` in the repo
- Do **not** execute it from Cursor; document one elevated command for the operator
